--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY ARITHMETIC reproduced exactly from the web source (cross-platform value parity,
NOT a "corrected" version)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  last trip     = trips[0]; recent list = trips.slice(0,3).slice(1) (shown only when length > 1);
                  overflow trips[3+] fetched (limit 5) but never displayed.
  distance      = convertDistanceFromSI(total_distance_m ?? 0, unitPref) [ /1000 km · /1609.344 mi ·
                  /0.3048 ft ] then fmtNumber(dist, 1)
  duration      = formatDurationRange(start_date, end_date)
                  [ '—' for missing endpoint / non-positive span ; else formatDurationMinutes(
                  round(ms/60000)) → 'Hh Mm' / 'Mm' ; a sub-30s span → '0m', a 30s span → '1m' ]
  drives/charge = fmtInt(drive_count ?? 0) / fmtInt(charge_count ?? 0)  [ grouped, locale-aware ]
  name          = name ?? 'Unnamed trip'  (JS `??` — only null falls back, empty string stays)
  date          = formatDateShort(start_date)  [ '—' for missing · locale+tz { month:'short',
                  day:'numeric' } ]
  isCompact     = size.cols <= 1 ; stat grid grid-cols-2 (compact) / grid-cols-4 (wide); recent-row
                  trailing meta (duration + drive badge) hidden when compact.

States reproduced (every one renders — no hidden surfaces):
  loading (skeleton card) · empty ("No trips recorded yet") · error (retry) · stale (chip + banner +
  auto-refresh) · offline (cached trips + banner) · content (last-trip card + recent list). Each has a
  #if DEBUG preview.

